---
title: Tension Balance Radar — Evaluation Circle
---
%% Each axis = one activated sense's evaluation score (1-10)
%% The polygon shape reveals balance:
%%   - Even polygon = healthy tension equilibrium
%%   - Dented polygon = one perspective is being sacrificed
%%   - Spiky polygon = over-optimizing some dimensions at others' expense

%% Mermaid doesn't natively do radar charts, so here's the conceptual structure:

graph TD
    subgraph "Radar Concept"
        CENTER((CENTER))

        CENTER --- |"8/10"| A["Color Harmony"]
        CENTER --- |"7/10"| B["Typography"]
        CENTER --- |"9/10"| C["Brand Voice"]
        CENTER --- |"6/10"| D["Accessibility"]
        CENTER --- |"8/10"| E["Call to Action"]
        CENTER --- |"5/10"| F["Spacing"]
        CENTER --- |"7/10"| G["Performance"]
    end

    subgraph "What the shape tells you"
        EVEN["Fat even polygon<br/>= balanced tension"]
        DENT["Dent on one axis<br/>= perspective sacrificed"]
        SPIKE["Spike on one axis<br/>= over-optimization"]
    end
